DOTr Undersecretary Timothy John Batan: Kasi kung mapapansin niyo po, yung mga pinaggastusan po nila to rehabilitate the existing system,

5779
04:15:17,620 --> 04:15:24,540
DOTr Undersecretary Timothy John Batan: to extend to Cavite, and to operate the line ay mas mataas po kumpara doon sa revenues pong nakolekta nila today.

5780
04:15:24,540 --> 04:15:33,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Again po, kung maaari pong makareceive po ng copy nung pinaggastahan na po ng nareceive na income ng LRMC.

5781
04:15:34,740 --> 04:15:40,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang tanong ko next po, sino pong legally mandated to ensure that the basic station facilities are maintained?

5782
04:15:40,700 --> 04:15:44,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Gaya po ng functional clean restrooms po. Is it LRMC po ba?

5783
04:15:46,440 --> 04:15:53,920
DOTr Undersecretary Timothy John Batan: LRMC po ang may responsibilidad dito at iyan po ay nakasaad sa concession agreement.

5784
04:15:53,920 --> 04:15:57,800
DOTr Undersecretary Timothy John Batan: Meron pong mga key performance indicators sa ating concession.

5785
04:15:58,480 --> 04:16:04,660
DOTr Undersecretary Timothy John Batan: At kung sakali po merong mga KPIs na hindi masusunod, ay nag-i-impose po tayo.

5786
04:16:04,780 --> 04:16:13,060
DOTr Undersecretary Timothy John Batan: Meron po tayong concession agreement management team sa LRTA na nag-i-impose po ng mga KPI penalties sa LRMC.

5787
04:16:14,360 --> 04:16:17,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At, and, siguro ang last question ko na lang po on this one,

5788
04:16:17,940 --> 04:16:23,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na pag-alaman ng representasyong ito na, unfortunately,

5789
04:16:23,920 --> 04:16:34,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: meron pong leaks, rain flooding inside the cars ng Gen 4 train sets even though they're brand new and taxpayer funded.

5790
04:16:35,520 --> 04:16:40,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, siguro ang tanong ko, bakit po ganito yung nangyayari?

5791
04:16:40,400 --> 04:16:45,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Bakit may ganitong leaks? Bakit may ganitong flooding despite it being brand new?

5792
04:16:49,400 --> 04:16:55,420
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Mr. Chair, yung pong latest po na incident na nagkaroon po ng tubig sa loob po ng train,

5793
04:16:55,820 --> 04:16:57,460
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: hindi po ito galing.

5794
04:16:57,500 --> 04:17:00,380
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Sa labas, hindi rin po ito problema sa roofing ng train.

5795
04:17:00,500 --> 04:17:01,880
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Ang nangyayari lang po is that,

5796
04:17:02,480 --> 04:17:06,500
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: nagka-problema po yung drainage nung kanilang aircon ng train.

5797
04:17:06,680 --> 04:17:12,260
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Kaya po yung tubig na nanggagaling po doon sa aircon, naipon po doon sa loob ng train.

5798
04:17:12,460 --> 04:17:15,940
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: At eventually, nung hindi na po gumagana yung drainage,

5799
04:17:16,080 --> 04:17:20,900
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: tumapon po sa loob ng train yung tubig na nanggagaling po sa aircon.

5800
04:17:20,900 --> 04:17:25,580
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: So, ang punot-dulo po is maintenance po.

5801
04:17:25,720 --> 04:17:27,040
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Kailangan lang pong linisin nila.

5802
04:17:27,500 --> 04:17:31,940
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Yung drainage or palitan po yung mga sirang parts doon sa drainage system po nung train.

5803
04:17:32,080 --> 04:17:34,900
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: At sinitan po namin ang LRMC.

5804
04:17:35,040 --> 04:17:38,560
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Actually, ito pong nakaraang incident, parang pangatlo na po yan.

5805
04:17:39,240 --> 04:17:42,820
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: At yung mga dalawang na unang incident, sinitan na po namin sila formally.

5806
04:17:43,280 --> 04:17:44,940
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Nakatatlong sulat na po kami sa kanila.

5807
04:17:45,600 --> 04:17:51,740
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: And doon po sa ibang mga bagay, like sa condition po ng mga CR nila, yung cleanliness po ng estasyon,

5808
04:17:52,340 --> 04:17:55,920
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: marami po tayong mga staff na nandoon, mga empleyado po ng LRT.

5809
04:17:55,920 --> 04:17:57,480
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: At binabantayan po namin sila.

5810
04:17:57,500 --> 04:18:01,980
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Actually, everyday po, nagbibigay kami ng citation sa mga violations po nila.

5811
04:18:02,220 --> 04:18:05,160
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Like maruming CR, maruming flooring. So lahat po.

5812
04:18:05,640 --> 04:18:09,140
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: In fact, under the concession agreement po, may penalty po sila.

5813
04:18:09,300 --> 04:18:16,180
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: So far, sa ngayon, ang kanilang penalty na sinisingil namin is umabot na po ng 121 million.

5814
04:18:16,780 --> 04:18:18,860
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Yun po yung outstanding na penalty po nila.

5815
04:18:19,540 --> 04:18:24,880
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Pero since meron po kami usapin tungkol sa mga utang naman natin sa kanila, nakapinbin po ito.

5816
04:18:24,880 --> 04:18:27,340
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Pero eventually po, isisingil po namin din.

5817
04:18:27,500 --> 04:18:30,680
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Itong amount na ito, galing po sa kanila.

5818
04:18:30,800 --> 04:18:35,380
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Kailangan po nilang bayaran or i-offset nila sa mga sinisingil po nila sa gobyerno.

5819
04:18:35,780 --> 04:18:35,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay.

5820
04:18:36,420 --> 04:18:45,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yun din po yung gusto nating maipunto na kung may accountability po dito, it would be LRMC.

5821
04:18:46,380 --> 04:18:53,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Meron pong concession agreement and then merong pag-insure na yung quality standards ay nasusunod.

5822
04:18:53,120 --> 04:18:57,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And so, natuwa ako na marinig na may ganong formal.

5823
04:18:57,500 --> 04:18:58,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Napag-sita.

5824
04:18:58,880 --> 04:19:10,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At mangingi po kami ng update, written update ng mga naging steps so far para po essentially i-hold accountable yung LRMC doon sa mga violations sa basic concession agreement.

5825
04:19:10,820 --> 04:19:16,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero sa atin, hindi po dapat yung low-level staff yung iberate.

5826
04:19:16,680 --> 04:19:18,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: It is dapat formally through LRMC.

5827
04:19:18,900 --> 04:19:21,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, mangingi po tayo ng kopya ng ganun kung maaari po, Mr. Chair.

5828
04:19:21,840 --> 04:19:23,720
LRTA Administrator Atty. Hernando T. Cabrera: Opo, ibibigay po namin po lahat.

5829
04:19:24,680 --> 04:19:27,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Siguro ang last questions ko na lang po ay it would be,

5830
04:19:27,500 --> 04:19:38,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in relation to NAIA, dahil po yun nga po in the past and in the recent years ay ito po ay binenta po sa NNIC.

5831
04:19:39,340 --> 04:19:49,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May question po tayo na, wait lang po Chair, pause lang po, saglit lang.

5832
04:19:57,880 --> 04:20:06,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pwede po bang malaman kung, Mr. Chair, magkano yung total na nakolekta ng NNIC sa mga passengers ng NAIA?

5833
04:20:06,060 --> 04:20:07,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this?

5834
04:20:07,900 --> 04:20:09,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Information that can be submitted?

5835
04:20:14,710 --> 04:20:18,730
DOTr Secretary Giovanni Z. Lopez: I think we're referring to passenger service charge po.

5836
04:20:19,210 --> 04:20:20,010
DOTr Secretary Giovanni Z. Lopez: Is that it po?

5837
04:20:20,170 --> 04:20:23,190
DOTr Secretary Giovanni Z. Lopez: The submission or the remittance of NNIC to the government.

5838
04:20:23,950 --> 04:20:31,190
DOTr Secretary Giovanni Z. Lopez: Kasi so far po, the NNIC remitted to the government around 78 billion pesos.

5839
04:20:33,410 --> 04:20:38,170
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Aside from the remittance po, andyan din po yung basically total na nakolek nila.

5840
04:20:38,850 --> 04:20:40,570
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Hindi lang din po sa passenger service charge.

5841
04:20:40,570 --> 04:20:45,570
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero lahat po nang nakolek nilang income ever since taking over NAIA.

5842
04:20:46,350 --> 04:20:52,490
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: It would include sana din po revenues sa lahat ng mga businesses and private operators sa NAIA.

5843
04:20:52,790 --> 04:21:02,390
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At ang mga nakita sa mga other operations sa NAIA, including din siyempre, other than concessionaires, yung mga aircraft carriers.

5844
04:21:02,610 --> 04:21:04,710
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can that be submitted, Mr. Chair?

5845
04:21:04,990 --> 04:21:06,430
DOTr Secretary Giovanni Z. Lopez: We will comply, Mr. Chair.

5846
04:21:07,030 --> 04:21:09,570
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, I ask this question dahil,

5847
04:21:10,570 --> 04:21:16,410
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: narinig na natin in other instances, yung magkano nang na-remit ng NNIC sa gobyerno.

5848
04:21:16,790 --> 04:21:25,550
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero hindi din po natin nakita yung other side of the picture, which is magkano na po ang income na nakuha nila since the purchase of NAIA through the passengers.

5849
04:21:26,110 --> 04:21:31,250
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Given nga po na nagkaroon ng passenger service charge increase, kailangan din natin po i-assess.

5850
04:21:31,950 --> 04:21:40,130
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Doon sa kung magkano yung na-remit and even kung magkano pa yung natitira na para matapos yung agreement.

5851
04:21:40,570 --> 04:21:43,850
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Magkano na ang nakuha in income?

5852
04:21:44,110 --> 04:21:52,270
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, we will be submitting informal letter na lang with the committee also furnished dun sa request po natin for data.

5853
04:21:52,390 --> 04:21:53,390
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

5854
04:21:57,640 --> 04:21:59,620
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: Thank you very much, Cong Renee Co.

5855
04:22:00,200 --> 04:22:07,760
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: Next to interpolate for the second round, and I hope this is the last, Representative Franz Pumaren.

5856
04:22:08,180 --> 04:22:09,100
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Yes, thank you very much.

5857
04:22:09,100 --> 04:22:10,860
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Actually, dapat hindi na ako magtatanong.

5858
04:22:11,020 --> 04:22:13,460
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Pero nandito na rin si GM.

5859
04:22:13,460 --> 04:22:14,760
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Sayang naman ang appearance niya.

5860
04:22:15,260 --> 04:22:21,140
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Diba, kung hindi natin tatanungin, I know, kayang-kaya ni Sec. Banoy sagutin to.

5861
04:22:21,740 --> 04:22:24,980
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Is this, there's still hope pa ba dun sa Bicol Express natin?

5862
04:22:26,200 --> 04:22:31,280
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Because I know yung loan natin with China will be expiring this year.

5863
04:22:31,520 --> 04:22:32,080
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Tama po ba?

5864
04:22:33,280 --> 04:22:36,360
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: With the permission of Sec. Banoy and Mr. Chair.

5865
04:22:37,840 --> 04:22:38,560
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Yes, sir.

5866
04:22:38,880 --> 04:22:39,920
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: There's still a hope.

5867
04:22:39,920 --> 04:22:42,960
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Actually, we're continuing yung rehabilitation pa rin.

5868
04:22:43,460 --> 04:22:48,600
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Yung line natin, yung dadalawa lang pong tren na nag-ooperate ngayon.

5869
04:22:48,780 --> 04:22:53,840
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Dito sa Lucena hanggang Calamba at saka sa Lupi, Camarines Sur hanggang Naga.

5870
04:22:54,480 --> 04:22:57,620
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Yung Naga to Legazpi was damaged last year due to the typhoon.

5871
04:22:58,120 --> 04:23:01,740
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: But we are restoring that with the budget that we have for 2026.

5872
04:23:02,340 --> 04:23:08,460
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: What we need to complete the 422-kilometer line is the rehabilitation po ng mula Lucena, Quezon.

5873
04:23:09,340 --> 04:23:11,580
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Idudugtong 'yun hanggang doon sa Lupi, Camarines Sur.

5874
04:23:11,580 --> 04:23:13,440
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: And those are the things na sinasama po

5875
04:23:13,460 --> 04:23:15,520
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: namin sa request ng budget sana.

5876
04:23:16,160 --> 04:23:22,820
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Which we hope the Congress, through the support of course of our Department of Transportation,

5877
04:23:23,400 --> 04:23:27,980
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: endorsing our request for additional budget para po sa capital outlay ng PNR po.

5878
04:23:28,600 --> 04:23:31,320
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: You know, alam ko yung sinasabi nyo, always there's hope.

5879
04:23:31,420 --> 04:23:34,400
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: But my main question ko dyan, is it worth the investment?

5880
04:23:34,640 --> 04:23:40,180
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: When in fact, do you have data kung ilan sumasakay ng papuntang Bicol Express?

5881
04:23:40,180 --> 04:23:43,140
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Because expiring na yung loan natin.

5882
04:23:43,460 --> 04:23:44,460
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: That's about 6 billion.

5883
04:23:44,740 --> 04:23:50,320
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Tapos, I guess you will be requesting Congress for additional funding.

5884
04:23:50,800 --> 04:23:53,980
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Do you think yung marirecover pa ba natin yung investment dyan?

5885
04:23:54,680 --> 04:23:56,700
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Do we have to look at the whole picture?

5886
04:23:57,960 --> 04:24:05,980
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Mr. Chair, ngayon po sa kasalukuyan, honestly, we have only around 1,600 daily ridership.

5887
04:24:06,400 --> 04:24:13,440
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: But with the migration of the trains na nung mga trains na nandito sa Manila na may migrate noong tumigil ang operasyon,

5888
04:24:13,460 --> 04:24:22,520
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: sa Manila, at idadagdag sa operasyon, that passenger is expected po na tataas po kami ng mga around 5,000 to 6,000 daily.

5889
04:24:23,100 --> 04:24:28,920
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: But with the additional trains po para sa Long Haul, I think, especially sa tourist destination pang Bicol,

5890
04:24:29,020 --> 04:24:34,000
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: connecting the Region 4 to Region 5, that will increase more passenger po.

5891
04:24:34,540 --> 04:24:39,540
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: At our expectation based doon sa study, initial study ng original alignment for South Long Haul,

5892
04:24:39,540 --> 04:24:43,160
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: passing through the original PNR alignment,

5893
04:24:43,460 --> 04:24:52,640
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: approximately around 20,000 to 25,000 daily ridership po ang pwede po mabigyan ng servisyo ng Philippine National Railway pa.

5894
04:24:52,940 --> 04:24:58,080
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Okay, ganito lang, GM. You can give me all those data, but we want it in writing.

5895
04:24:58,260 --> 04:25:07,140
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: So before we bring this to the plenary, if you can submit us all the data, justification, is it worth investing,

5896
04:25:07,140 --> 04:25:11,080
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: is it worth pushing yung proyektong yan? Okay?

5897
04:25:12,180 --> 04:25:13,140
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Mr. Chair, yes.

5898
04:25:13,460 --> 04:25:18,540
PNR General Manager Deovanni S. Miranda: Yes, we will submit po, of course, in coordination to our Secretary Banay po.

5899
04:25:18,960 --> 04:25:22,940
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Okay, next, yung paborito ko, Marina. Okay.

5900
04:25:24,300 --> 04:25:29,220
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Kamusta yung Orient Register Classification? Suspended na ba yun? Blacklisted na ba yun?

5901
04:25:30,340 --> 04:25:34,880
MARINA Administrator Sonia B. Malaluan: Mr. Chair, still suspended pa po under the preventive suspension.

5902
04:25:35,640 --> 04:25:39,940
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: So, alam ko suspended. I'm just trying to ask your opinion. Blacklisted na ba yun?

5903
04:25:39,940 --> 04:25:42,740
MARINA Administrator Sonia B. Malaluan: Not yet po. So, meron pa pong...

5904
04:25:43,460 --> 04:25:46,100
MARINA Administrator Sonia B. Malaluan: Still, actually, nasa Office of the President.

5905
04:25:46,360 --> 04:25:48,100
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: You know, sino may appeal? Sila?

5906
04:25:48,300 --> 04:25:48,760
MARINA Administrator Sonia B. Malaluan: Sila po.

5907
04:25:49,140 --> 04:25:54,320
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: But who will give the recommendation? It's Marina, right? Hindi naman alam ng Presidente yan eh.

5908
04:25:54,960 --> 04:25:59,860
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: So, ang point ko dito, why is this Orient Classification is so special?

5909
04:26:00,340 --> 04:26:04,360
Rep. Franz S. Pumaren: Ilan palpak na to? Ilan na namatay na tao na hindi natin blacklist?

